  "equipment_policy": "New eligible humanoid monsters only; persist each spawn decision including empty results. Ordinary dates use one whole-set acceptance/material roll for empty slots. From the second blood moon, blood dates independently roll acceptance and material for each empty slot; mixed materials and missing pieces are allowed. Copper and silver are peer materials with half their shared grade weight each. From the eighth actual blood moon (day 320), use highest basis stage 8. Preserve fixed sets, explicit equipment, drop rates and source generated quality/wear/enchantments. First blood date preserves legacy materials and partial armor; existing saved monsters never reroll.",
  "ordinary_held_probability": "(40 + 5 * ordinaryProgress) / 100",
  "blood_held_probability": "(70 + 3 * stage) / 100",
  "held_equipment_policy": "Applicable melee humanoids with an empty main hand only; preserve existing weapons and ranged mobs. Draw held-equipment acceptance separately from armor. Prefer the first armor piece newly filled in head/chest/legs/feet order, otherwise recognize existing armor, otherwise draw an independent material. Sword, pickaxe, shovel and axe have equal type weights; leather/chain tiers fall back to rusted iron tools.",
